  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A muon, created due to cosmic rays in the upper atmosphere, is travelling at a speed of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.99c\"></span>. The distance between the upper atmosphere and the surface of Earth, as measured in the reference frame of Earth, is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10\\;\\textup{km}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the best estimate for the distance between the upper atmosphere and the surface of Earth as measured in the muon’s reference frame?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.8\\;\\textup{km}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.4\\;\\textup{km}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\\;\\textup{km}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.2\\;\\textup{km}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
